            oa:hasSelector [ a oa:TextQuoteSelector ;
                oa:exact "You want to tightly control the unit of expand. What I don't want is, if you're trying to get a call, the unit of expand is the call, right, or the memory. You don't want to get a single position. I might even go so far as to say that you don't want to let a single position be expanded. You want it always to be under a narrative or call or another door, because, to the point of steering, not retrieval, we don't want to just return a single position. We want to return the context around it." ;
